PARAMETERS
==========

p      = success probability
n      = number of trials
r      = number of successes (Negative Binomial)
         or shape parameter (Gamma)

λ      = rate parameter
μ      = mean
σ²     = variance
σ      = standard deviation

α, β   = Beta shape parameters
k      = Weibull shape parameter

N      = population size
K      = successes in population
ρ      = K/N

ν      = degrees of freedom


SUPPORTS
========

Bernoulli(p)            {0,1}
Binomial(n,p)           {0,1,...,n}
Poisson(λ)              {0,1,2,...}
Geometric(p)            {0,1,2,...}
Negative Binomial(r,p)  {0,1,2,...}

Uniform(a,b)            a ≤ x ≤ b
Beta(α,β)               0 ≤ x ≤ 1
Exponential(λ)          x ≥ 0
Gamma(r,λ)              x ≥ 0
Weibull(k,λ)            x ≥ 0

Normal(μ,σ²)            -∞ < x < ∞
Lognormal(μ,σ²)         x > 0
Chi-Squared(ν)          x ≥ 0
Cauchy(0,1)             -∞ < x < ∞


FUNDAMENTALS
============

Bernoulli(p)
  Mean = p
  Var  = p(1-p)

Binomial(n,p)
  Mean = np
  Var  = np(1-p)

Poisson(λ)
  Mean = λ
  Var  = λ

Geometric(p)
  Mean = (1-p)/p
  Var  = (1-p)/p²

Negative Binomial(r,p)
  Mean = r(1-p)/p
  Var  = r(1-p)/p²

Uniform(a,b)
  Mean = (a+b)/2
  Var  = (b-a)²/12

Exponential(λ)
  Mean = 1/λ
  Var  = 1/λ²

Gamma(r,λ)
  Mean = r/λ
  Var  = r/λ²

Normal(μ,σ²)
  Mean = μ
  Var  = σ²

Normal(0,1)
  Mean = 0
  Var  = 1

Beta(α,β)
  Mean = α/(α+β)
  Var  = αβ/[(α+β)²(α+β+1)]

Chi-Squared(ν)
  Mean = ν
  Var  = 2ν

Cauchy(0,1)
  Mean = undefined
  Var  = undefined

Weibull(k,λ)
  Flexible lifetime / reliability model


KEY RELATIONSHIPS
=================

Bernoulli --ΣX--> Binomial

Geometric --ΣX--> Negative Binomial

Exponential --ΣX--> Gamma

Gamma(r=1, λ) = Exponential(λ)

Beta(1,1) = Uniform(0,1)

Hypergeometric ≈ Binomial
  when n/N ≤ 0.05

Poisson ≈ Binomial
  when λ = np

Binomial → Normal
  n → ∞, p fixed

Poisson → Normal
  λ → ∞

Lognormal ⇄ Normal
  via exp(.) and log(.)

Z = (X-μ)/σ
X = μ + σZ

ΣZi² ~ Chi-Squared(ν)

Z1/Z2 ~ Cauchy(0,1)

U = e^(-λX)
X = -ln(U)/λ

If X1 ~ Gamma(α,λ) and X2 ~ Gamma(β,λ)

    X1
  -------  ~ Beta(α,β)
  X1 + X2


