CENTRAL IDEA
============

Aggregation equalizes randomness.

Many counting processes:
  Bernoulli -> Binomial -> Normal
  Geometric -> Negative Binomial -> Poisson -> Normal

Many waiting-time processes:
  Exponential -> Gamma

Many transformations:
  Normal <-> Lognormal
  Normal -> Chi-Squared
  Normal -> Cauchy

Normal is the central attractor of probability theory,
appearing through limits, sums, approximations, and
transformations.
